    <Program class="ca.nrcan.gc.OEE.ERS.ErsProgram">
        <Labels>
            <English>EnerGuide Rating System</English>
            <French>Syst??????me de cote ??????nerGuide</French>
        </Labels>
        <Version major="15" minor="10" build="20288">
            <Labels>
                <English>v15.10b20288</English>
                <French>v15.10b20288</French>
            </Labels>
        </Version>
        <SdkVersion major="1" minor="16" build="20288">
            <Labels>
                <English>v1.16b20288</English>
                <French>v1.16b20288</French>
            </Labels>
        </SdkVersion>
        <Options>
            <Main applyHouseholdOperatingConditions="false" applyReducedOperatingConditions="false" atypicalElectricalLoads="false" waterConservation="true" referenceHouse="false">
                <Vermiculite code="3">
                    <English>No Vermiculite</English>
                    <French>Pas de Vermiculite</French>
                </Vermiculite>
            </Main>
            <WaterConservation LowFlushToilets="0" LowFlushToiletsUpgrade="0" />
            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>The infiltration test shows a high level of air leakage in the house. A high level of air leakage lead you to a high level of heat loss and therefore an increase of the cost and the energy required to heat the interior space.</airSeal>
                <mainWalls>After evalution we estimate the insulation of the house to be R-12, which is not enough. We recommend to reach the actual standard R-28 or even R-30,  by the addition of insulation.  We recommend to insulate from outside, this technique will help to increase the airtightness of the building envelope. 



This technique will also avoid the reduction of space inside the house.

</mainWalls>
                <ceilings>The actual attic insulation is R-31. This level of insulation is also under the actual standard which is R-60. We recommend the addition of insulation to meet the standard.



The addition of insulation will contribute to fight against the heat loss through the roof during the heating season, and in the opposite in summer time to reduce the overheating of the upper floor.</ceilings>
                <exposedFloors>In this moment we estimate the insulation to be R-20, we suggest the addition of insulation to reach a level of R-30.</exposedFloors>
                <windows>During the infiltration test we notice that the window located beside the main entrance door leaks and the frame show signs of fatigue. We recommend the replacement of the window by an ENERGY STAR unit that meet the northern climate standard.</windows>
                <VentilationSystem>If you proceed to the re-insulation of the house, the building should be more air tight. This situation will increase the level of humidity inside the house and a possible reduction of the air quality of the house.



We recommend the installation of an HRV (Heat Recovery Ventilator) Energy Star certified and also HVI (Home Ventilation Institute) certified.</VentilationSystem>
                <HotWaterSystem>During the evaluation we were unable to verify the domestic water heater, because it was wrapped by some insulation.</HotWaterSystem>
                <HeatingSystem>During the evaluation the home owner mention the intention of adding a secondary heating system in order to reduce the utilisation of the electric heating.

We recommend to install a Heat Pump because of the efficiency of the system. This kind of equipment can produce 3 times more energy than a typical baseboard. Therefore this type system can't run when the temperatures are lower than -25 degrees celcius. This system can also provide cooling during summer.



The installation of this equipment remain a personal decision from the home owner.



Befeore installing a new heating system, the air tightness of the house must be fixed, otherwise it won't be efficient.</HeatingSystem>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
